\section{DataOM}{

\code{DataOM} passes true operating model quantities to MPs, for example to
build reference or "perfect information" MPs. The selected slots of the
\link[=hist-class]{hist} object are added to \code{Data@Misc$DataOM} (a \link[=hist-class]{hist}
object subset to the current simulation) each time the MP is called.

Any slot of \link[=hist-class]{hist} except \code{Data} can be requested, e.g.
\code{Reference}, \code{Unfished}, \code{Number}, \code{Biomass}, \code{SBiomass}, \code{Landings},
\code{Effort}, \code{FDead}. \code{DataOM} accepts:
\itemize{
\item \code{TRUE}: all slots.
\item A character vector of slot names, e.g. \code{c('Biomass', 'Number')}.
\item A named logical list, e.g. \code{list(Biomass = TRUE, Number = TRUE)}.
Elements set to \code{FALSE} are not included.
}

In \code{OM@Control$DataOM}, elements named after a \link[=hist-class]{hist} slot apply to
every MP. Any other element name is treated as the name of an MP, and its
value (in any of the forms above, or \code{FALSE}) applies to that MP only:

\if{html}{\out{<div class="sourceCode r">}}\preformatted{Control(OM)$DataOM <- TRUE                               # all slots, every MP
Control(OM)$DataOM <- c('Biomass', 'Number')             # these slots, every MP
Control(OM)$DataOM <- list(Reference = TRUE,             # every MP
                           myMP = c('Biomass', 'Number'),# myMP only
                           MP2  = FALSE)                 # nothing for MP2
}\if{html}{\out{</div>}}

MP functions can also request slots with a \code{DataOM} attribute, in the
same forms:

\if{html}{\out{<div class="sourceCode r">}}\preformatted{attr(myMP, 'DataOM') <- c('Reference', 'Biomass')
}\if{html}{\out{</div>}}

The slots passed to an MP are:
\itemize{
\item the MP's entry in \code{OM@Control$DataOM}, if there is one;
\item otherwise, the union of the OM-wide slots in \code{OM@Control$DataOM} and
the MP's \code{DataOM} attribute.
}

MP-specific entries are matched against the MP names used in
\code{\link[=Project]{Project()}}. \code{\link[=TuneMP]{TuneMP()}} projects renamed copies of the MP, so use the MP
attribute or OM-wide slots for MPs that are tuned.

During projections, time-series slots (e.g. \code{Number}, \code{Biomass},
\code{Landings}, \code{Effort}) include only the time steps before the one the
advice applies to (\code{Data@Misc$AdviceYear}). \code{OM}, \code{Unfished}, and
\code{Reference} are passed in full.

The reference MPs (see \link{ReferenceMPs}) set
\code{attr(MP, 'DataOM') <- list(Reference = TRUE)}. An MP that calls one of
them internally needs \code{Reference} too, either from its own \code{DataOM}
attribute or from \code{OM@Control$DataOM}.
}

\section{Internal settings}{

\code{Clone}, \code{CalcCatchAtSizeNeeded}, and \code{CalcCatchAtSizeCpp} are set
internally by \code{\link[=Simulate]{Simulate()}} and should not be modified.
}

\examples{
\dontrun{
OM <- SingleStockOM
Control(OM)$MSYType <- 'Landings'
Control(OM)$DataOM  <- list(Reference = TRUE)

myMP <- function(Data) {
  B <- Data@Misc$DataOM@Biomass
  refFMSY(Data)
}
class(myMP) <- 'mp'
attr(myMP, 'DataOM') <- 'Biomass'

Hist <- Simulate(OM)
MSE  <- Project(Hist, MPs = c('refFMSY', 'myMP'))
}
}
